{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>You shall not abominate an Edomite.</b> Even though it is fitting for you to abominate him because he came out with the sword against you, and the Egyptians likewise — even though they cast your males into the Nile — you shall not abominate them, because they were your hosts in the time of distress and you took refuge with them in the years of famine, with great honor. And it further says, 'You shall not abominate an Edomite,' because they have the merit of the fathers, for they were of holy seed; and He distanced them three generations because they came out with the sword against us. And it says of both of them, לא תתעב — 'you shall not abominate': Edom, who preceded with the sword, and Egypt, who drowned them in water; but Ammon and Moab, who caused them to sin, are abominated, and Scripture says of them, לא תדרוש שלומם וטובתם — 'you shall not seek their peace and their good.' From this the Rabbis, of blessed memory, derived that anyone who causes his fellow to sin — it is worse for him than one who kills him: one who kills him removes him from this world, but one who causes him to sin removes him from this world and from the World to Come."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:50:33.770779418Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}